-- cmd: fmt
-- A carriage return in front of a line end's own one is the comment's
-- text: it stays, and so does that line end (written as a line feed
-- alone, the next pass would drop the carriage return). The fuzz case:
-- the formatter lost one on every pass.
fn main() {
  {- a
  b -}
  println(1)
}

{- c
d -}
